# Keep the build context small and free of host/runtime artifacts.
# Only requirements.txt, db_ops/, and docker/entrypoint.sh are COPYed by the Dockerfile.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.pytest_tmp/
tmp_pytest_local/
tests/
docs/
logs/
runtime/
*.log
.venv/
node_modules/
*.sqlite
# Runtime inputs are bind-mounted, not baked in.
config.json
config.*.json
data/
# The OPERATOR's assets only — task SQL and bot commands, bind-mounted at runtime rather than
# baked in. The shipped half lives with the component that owns it (db_ops/metrics/collectors,
# db_ops/common/{backup,restore}_scripts, db_ops/sre/host_config) and ships
# inside the image with the package, so the leading slash matters: it anchors this to the root.
/assets/
# The legacy Oracle 8i tool: a Win32 Python 2.7 runtime and ~200MB of Oracle 10.2 client DLLs
# that cannot execute on Linux anyway. The Dockerfile never COPYs it, but the build context is
# the whole repo, so without this every `build-image` ships ~370MB to the daemon for nothing.
tools/
